=== 500-AFTER-COMMIT INVESTIGATION (current code, fresh harness, ephemeral port) ===
Question: batch-1 run 2 returned 5x500 while 5 redemptions + subs committed.
Method: 3 runs (A/B/C), each with a new disposable user + VERIFY- code
(maxUsesPerAccount=1), 5 concurrent POST /api/promo-codes/redeem, then full
fixture cleanup per run. Harness stdout/stderr captured; emails and raw
tokens below are redacted (accounts deleted afterwards in every run).

--- run A ---
register: status=201
create-code: status=201
successes=1 of=5
  200:ok
  400:PROMO_CODE_ALREADY_USED (x4)
redemption-rows=1, user-subscriptions=1
cleanup: reds=1 subs=1 pays=0, delete-me: status=200

--- run B ---
successes=1 of=5, 200:ok + 4x 400:PROMO_CODE_ALREADY_USED,
redemption-rows=1, cleanup full, delete-me: status=200

--- run C ---
successes=1 of=5, 200:ok + 4x 400:PROMO_CODE_ALREADY_USED,
redemption-rows=1, cleanup full, delete-me: status=200

--- harness console (redacted; 3 boot+register cycles, same shape each) ---
throwaway listening port=<ephemeral>
[DEV] Verification token for <redacted-email>: <redacted-token>
[email] RESEND_API_KEY not set — skipping verification email to <redacted-email>
(no stacks, no error lines in stdout or stderr across all 3 runs)

--- timeout/maxWait config ---
No explicit timeout/maxWait on the promo $transaction
(src/routes/promoCodes.routes.ts) or the Prisma client (src/lib/prisma.ts);
engine defaults apply. Not implicated: no timeout error surfaced anywhere.

=== CONCLUSION: NOT REPRODUCED on current code ===
15 concurrent redemptions across 3 runs: zero 500s, zero stacks, exact
1+4x400 + 1 row every time. The batch-1 500-after-commit mechanism is
UNDETERMINED: pre-fix race proven separately (5/5 + 5 rows, run 1), the
run-2 500s hit pre-fix code served by a stale harness (restarted only
afterwards) with writes demonstrably committed, so the throw site was after
commit (response path) or pooler/harness-state related — but no evidence
remains to pin it, and the void-column $queryRaw theory is excluded (that
edit never executed on any harness; the probe that found it ran standalone).
All batch-1 fixture rows were identified and removed; counts restored
(users aside: soft-deleted disposables retained by design).
